          "path": "_m/g/c/e/q/lough-neagh-wp/bantam-tug-lough-neagh-geograp.jpg",
          "filename": "Bantam tug, Lough Neagh - geograph.org.uk - 857031.jpg",
          "caption": "Bantam tug, Lough Neagh More than 90 of the 25ft Bantam tugs were built for use on inland waterways.  Few survive and fewer still survive to serve their original purpose.  This one Bantam 2 is used to tow a sand barge in the event of a breakdown on Lough Neagh.  Built in 1955.  Usually kept at this small cut (not shown on the OS map).  Taken on private property by kind consent.",
          "alt": "Bantam tug, Lough Neagh More than 90 of the 25ft Bantam tugs were built for use on inland waterways.  Few survive and fewer still survive to serve their original purpose.  This one Bantam 2 is used to tow a sand barge in the event of a breakdown on Lough Neagh.  Built in 1955.  Usually kept at this small cut (not shown on the OS map).  Taken on private property by kind consent.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 413,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
