        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/e/q/lough-neagh-wp/former-coal-barge-lough-neagh-.jpg",
          "filename": "Former coal barge, Lough Neagh - geograph.org.uk - 857071.jpg",
          "caption": "Former coal barge, Lough Neagh. See 802692.  This is another of the Kelly's barges to have found its way to Lough Neagh.  It was used in the sand trade being loaded by grab and towed to the shore for discharge.  Although looking like a hulk it still seems to be afloat.  The original fleet number is thought to have been JK7.  Taken on private property by kind consent.",
